{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "strict": true,
    // Three flags beyond `strict`, all measured before being turned on: each cost zero or
    // near-zero to adopt. `noUnusedLocals` immediately found seven dead imports, which is the
    // same class of defect a manual scan had just found in `sizing.ts` -- worth having a
    // compiler do rather than a person.
    //
    // Two more were measured and NOT adopted, with the cost recorded rather than the decision
    // hidden: `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` (25 errors) and `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
    // (208 errors). Both are real improvements; neither is a change to make at the end of a
    // session, and an unmeasured "we should turn these on someday" is how they never get
    // turned on. The numbers are the entry criteria.
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    // ajv-formats is CJS with `export =`; without interop its default import is not
    // callable under NodeNext. Vitest's transform already does this at runtime, so
    // this makes the typechecker agree with what actually executes.
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    // The three checker scripts are plain .mjs and the suite imports them. Inferring
    // their types from the source beats hand-written .d.mts files, which are one more
    // thing that can silently stop matching. checkJs stays off: these are scripts, and
    // turning it on would be a separate piece of work with its own error list.
    "allowJs": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  // Every TypeScript file in the repo. The previous list named only core, contracts
  // and scripts/*.mjs, so `npm run typecheck` silently skipped the Application layer,
  // both adapters, the CLI, the whole test suite, and the differential oracle —
  // roughly two thirds of the TypeScript, inside a command named `typecheck` that
  // `npm run verify` depends on. Probed by planting a type error in each location:
  // five of seven were unchecked.
  //
  // `sources/**` is excluded deliberately: it is frozen prior art, not this project's
  // code, and it must never be edited to satisfy a compiler here.
  "include": [
    "contracts/**/*.ts",
    "core/**/*.ts",
    "application/**/*.ts",
    "adapters/**/*.ts",
    "shells/**/*.ts",
    "test/**/*.ts",
    "scripts/**/*.ts",
    "scripts/**/*.mjs"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "sources",
    "**/node_modules"
  ]
}
